{title: A Gift For All}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 123}

Verse 1
[G]See the people as they rush all around;
Every [GMaj7]store in the town
selling [Bm]toys to go under the [D]tree.[Dsus] [D]
[G]Every corner has a red-suited man
with a [GMaj7]bell in his hand,
And the [Bm]sights are something to [D]see. [Dsus] [D]
[C]But beneath all the [D]noise,
they can find the true [Bm]meaning of [Em]Christmas:
[C]Jesus came to the [D]earth, a gift from heaven a-[Bm]bove. [Em]
[C]Far beyond all the [D]toys,
they can find the true [Bm]meaning of [Em]Christmas:
[D]Jesus came to the earth, with forgiveness and love.
[D7]As a gift for [G]all! [D]

Verse 2
[G]See the families as they all gather near,
Full of [GMaj7]holiday cheer,
as the [Bm]lights flash bright red and [D]green.[Dsus] [D]
[G]Turkey, dressing, and some fresh apple pie
put a [GMaj7]gleam in your eye,
It's more [Bm]fun than you've ever [D]seen. [Dsus] [D]
[C]But beneath all the [D]noise,
they can find the true [Bm]meaning of [Em]Christmas:
[C]Jesus came to the [D]earth, a gift from heaven a-[Bm]bove. [Em]
[C]Far beyond all the [D]toys,
they can find the true [Bm]meaning of [Em]Christmas:
[D]Jesus came to the earth, with forgiveness and love.
[D7]As a gift for [G]all!

Chorus
[D]Come, let me tell you of the [G]One
[GMaj7]From heaven a-[G7]bove
Came as a [C]humble child to [Am]Bethlehem;
[G]Thanks be unto [D]Him!
Tell of the [G]One
[GMaj7]From heaven a-[G7]bove
Came to show [C]Truth and Love in [Am]every way,
[G]Turn our darkness [Em]into Day;
[Am]That's what Christmas [D]truly means to [G]me!
